{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777679827,"nonce":"d6L6VCWTf3LXtvA/XEDViB2QO6Q=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABBE2uQA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124","origin":"github"},"title":"Post-mission data review — 2026-05-01 BizzyBoat deployment","message":"## Post-mission data review — 2026-05-01 BizzyBoat deployment\n\nPart of #121.\n\nThe 2026-05-01 deployment recorded a long bag covering five hours\non-water with extensive saturation / fault / recovery events. This\nissue tracks the post-mission analysis work: extract the\nquantitative data, validate hypotheses formed in the moment, and\nturn observations into durable performance specs / follow-up issues.\n\n## Context\n\n- **Deployment issue**: #121\n- **Dev log**: [`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_dev_logs.md`](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_dev_logs.md)\n  (open in PR — wrap-up PR for #121 still TBD)\n- **gabby log**: [`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_gabby_logs.md`](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_gabby_logs.md)\n  (in [#123](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/123))\n- **salmon log**: [`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_salmon_logs.md`](docs/logs/2026/2026-05-01_salmon_logs.md)\n  (in [#123](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/123))\n- **Field-import PRs**:\n  - [rolker/marine_tools#9](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/9)\n  - [rolker/udp_bridge#16](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/pull/16)\n  - [rolker/camp#51](https://github.com/rolker/camp/pull/51)\n  - [#123](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/123)\n\n## Review areas\n\n### 1. Networking / `udp_bridge`\n\n- [ ] Per-topic discarded-packet counts — which topics dominated drops?\n- [ ] Rate-vs-distance correlation — does latency grow linearly or step at specific link transitions?\n- [ ] Path attribution per minute — WiFi / Starlink / cellular?  (Feeds the VPN-path-indicator follow-up.)\n- [ ] Latency-event characterization — 30 s and 60 s \"all red\" episodes: queue-depth growth, drop attribution.\n- [ ] Resend-layer activity — was the 5 s resend window firing? How often, on which topics? Confirm or rule out as the heartbeat 30 s alternation cause.\n- [ ] Bridge bandwidth vs. configured cap — when did the rate limiter actually fire vs. the link being naturally saturated?\n- [ ] Kernel UDP drops on gabby (gabby log §9) — confirm the 17k since-boot count and validate the sysctl tuning hypothesis.\n\n### 2. Performance characterization\n\n- [ ] **Max reverse speed** — extract steady-state from the ~18:40 full-reverse window; record in `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_hardware.md` (or appropriate performance-specs doc).\n- [ ] Max forward speed (steady state) — likely from the longer run after `FS_THR_ENABLE = 0` was in place.\n- [ ] Acceleration / deceleration profiles.\n- [ ] Turn radius / line-transition behavior from the multi-line track.\n- [ ] Course-keeping (XTE) on straight legs.\n- [ ] **Speed vs PWM** correlation across all line bearings.\n- [ ] Resolve the **1.5 m/s commanded but tracked ~1.0 m/s** observation — current opposing motion, throttle saturation, or autonomy-side cap?\n\n### 3. Power\n\n- [ ] Battery voltage at launch (13:36 EDT).\n- [ ] Battery voltage at recovery (18:42 EDT).\n- [ ] Voltage sag under load — max-reverse moment, line-transition turns.\n\n*Voltage only; BizzyBoat has no current meter — `BatteryState.current` is a placeholder.*\n\n### 4. Autonomy / BT\n\n- [ ] **Forensic match of gabby log §11** — count `FollowPath` ABORTs and confirm `SkipUnknownTaskType` catchall fires that marked tracklines done.\n- [ ] **15:09 HOLD-episode reconstruction** — exact timeline; did `done_hover` fire as predicted?\n- [ ] Mode transition history — full GUIDED ↔ LOITER ↔ MANUAL transitions, correlated with RC channel reads and operator commands.\n- [ ] Goto override timeline — success vs. fail intervals, correlated with FCU mode at command time. Compare 13:59 (no response) vs. 15:27 (worked).\n\n### 5. SBG vs FCU comparison\n\n- [ ] Position agreement at `bizzy/base_link` — quantify (mean, RMS, max).\n- [ ] Velocity comparison (linear, angular).\n- [ ] Attitude / heading agreement.\n- [ ] Altitude after applying gabby log §2.7 geoid-model translation — expect ~11 cm at WGS84 ellipsoidal.\n- [ ] Time-domain alignment — quantify residual offset between SBG and FCU clocks (both UTC-disciplined).\n\n### 6. Sonar / time-sync\n\n- [ ] M3 PPS pulse count over the full run (M3 software Output Messages log).\n- [ ] ZDA ↔ PPS pairing — `preLDINF ZDA` + `PPS [timestamp] latched` lines, verify all paired correctly.\n- [ ] Sound speed sensor data continuity / sanity.\n- [ ] M3 bottom detections — was the M3 actually pinging usefully through the run?\n\n### 7. Perception\n\n- [ ] **Mooring ball near-miss** (14:21) — does the segmentation pipeline detect it in post? Confirms the perception→costmap follow-up is feasible.\n- [ ] Camera frame stats — drops, latency, encoder bitrate vs. effective rate.\n- [ ] Segmentation detection rates / false positives.\n\n### 8. Comms-loss recovery\n\n- [ ] 3-min Starlink outage (14:28–14:31) — confirm which path actually carried traffic during the gap (cellular suspected).\n- [ ] CAMP UI behaviors during outages — characterize widget stall behavior.\n\n### 9. Operator UX\n\n- [ ] CAMP UI Standby state lag — was the 15:13 issue pure UI display, or was the underlying mode change actually slow to propagate?\n- [ ] NavSource matching events — when did per-platform topics start/stop flowing to CAMP?\n\n## Output\n\nEach finding from this review should produce one of:\n\n- A measured value committed to the appropriate spec doc (e.g., `bizzyboat_hardware.md`).\n- A new issue against the appropriate repo (perception→costmap, BT catchall fix, sysctl tuning, etc.).\n- An update to the relevant design doc.\n- A close on a related follow-up flagged in the dev log.\n\nUpdates land in this issue's comments as work progresses; issue closes when all checkboxes are complete or have been spun out into other tracked work.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}